<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>The 5 false positives where GPT 5.1 with reasoning gave a relevance rating of 3, while the human annotations gave a relevance of 0. While many passages are partially relevant, we believe they do not fully answer the query and should receive a lower rating. All other 89 ‘false positives’ are due to mistakes in the annotations, not mistakes of the LLM-RJS. </figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Reasoning experiment with GPT-OSS</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Figure <a href="#A3.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ Appendix C Reasoning experiment with GPT-OSS ‣ Why Large Language Models can Secretly Outperform Embedding Similarity in Information Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> we reproduce Experiment 2 with an open-source reasoning model. Again we see that the model is more likely to give higher relevance ratings than the humans, and that this effect is larger for the reasoning model. Compared to GPT 5.1, we do see an increase in false-negatives (lower triangular) suggesting that this model might also have generally increased errors.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F6" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A3.F6.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2603.08077v1/cm_no_reasoning_gpt_oss.png" id="A3.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:231/236;" width="231" height="236" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A3.F6.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2603.08077v1/cm_reasoning_gpt_oss.png" id="A3.F6.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:203/236;" width="203" height="236" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Differences between human and LLM relevance ratings with and without reasoning for GPT 5.1. The LLMs overall are more likely to see relevance in documents, especially with reasoning.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
